          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-113781",
          ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[4]{x}-{x}^{5}.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[4]{x}-{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{1/4}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{1/4+1}}{(\\frac{1}{4}+1)}-\\frac{{x}^{5+1}}{(5+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{\\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{(6)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt[4]{{x}^{5}}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
