          ":question/id": "79aa6724-ce36-5977-907b-506fab54c4d7",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-71169",
          ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}+4.$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}+4\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}x+4\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-3/2}\\text{d}x+4\\int {x}^{0}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3/2+1}}{(-\\frac{3}{2}+1)}+4\\left(\\frac{{x}^{0+1}}{0+1}\\right)+C \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {x}^{-1/2}+4x+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+4x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
        {
          ":db/id": 17592186234303,
          ":question/difficulty": {
            ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
          },
          ":question/id": "09d58888-0116-53f3-b47a-9d0d7153229f",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-71173",
          ":question/problem": "$\\int 2+\\frac{1}{{y}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y=$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2+\\frac{1}{{y}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int 1\\,\\text{d}y+\\int {y}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\int {y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y+\\int {y}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{{y}^{0+1}}{0+1}\\right)+\\frac{{y}^{-5+1}}{-5+1}+C \\\\  & =2y+\\frac{{y}^{-4}}{-4}+C \\\\  & =2y-\\frac{1}{4{y}^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        },
