          ":question/id": "9e4827b1-c8af-5e0e-a92c-bab0c6f19c7d",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-71167",
          ":question/problem": "$\\int 5-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int {x}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\left(\\frac{{x}^{0+1}}{0+1}\\right)-\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1}+C \\\\  & =5x-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        }
