              ":db/id": 17592186184058,
              ":question/id": "ea7dadee-2b44-5e62-bef4-26fb0cb185ea",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-372",
              ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int 2 x^3 - x \\,\\textrm d x.$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{3}-x\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{{x}^{1+1}}{1+1}\\right)+C \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "a58c0a18-4221-50f1-b31c-ae58d099d79d",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186184155,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186184059,
              ":question/id": "8f99b603-2fba-5a58-9966-b91d3a8a773e",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-373",
              ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left( 5(\\sqrt{x})^{3} - 4 x^2 + 5\\right) \\,\\textrm d x.$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5(\\sqrt{x})^{3}-4{x}^{2}+5)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5{x}^{3/2}-4{x}^{2}+5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {x}^{2}\\text{d}x+5\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\left(\\frac{{x}^{5/2}}{\\frac{5}{2}}\\right)-4\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)+5(x)+C \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}+5x+C \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}+5x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "007f3355-427a-5da4-8af7-22581f1cb1de",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Integrating Sums of Power Functions"
          }
        ],
